A-4 / A-5 — keyboard + focus, reasoning from the markup + CSS:
  No `tabindex` attribute anywhere in the changed partial (only pre-existing
  `tabindex="-1"` on #file-list, untouched). DOM order per row is
  checkbox -> label (not focusable) -> select, matching visual order, so
  default browser tab order is already correct; no positive tabindex to
  create a trap or skip.
  Disabled checkboxes (`{{if or $e.Exists $e.IdenticalTo}}disabled{{end}}`)
  render the real HTML `disabled` boolean attribute (confirmed in scan.html
  output: `<input ... disabled class="...disabled:opacity-60">`) — genuinely
  non-focusable/non-operable, not merely styled; `disabled:opacity-60` is
  the Tailwind `:disabled` pseudo-class variant riding the real attribute,
  not an independent visual-only fake.
  Focus indicator: neither the new `<select>` nor the pre-existing checkbox
  carries its own focus-ring/outline-none Tailwind classes beyond
  `focus:ring-2 focus:ring-accent` (checkbox, pre-existing) and
  `focus:ring-accent focus:border-accent` (new select) — both resolve
  through the sitewide rule in web/static/css/styles.css:
    input:focus, select:focus, textarea:focus {
      outline: none; box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px rgb(var(--accent));
    }
  --accent (styles.css): light rgb(79,70,229) / dark rgb(165,180,252).
  Ring contrast: light 6.29:1 vs white; dark 5.15:1 vs the select's own
  gray-700 fill, 7.61:1 vs the card's gray-800 background — both ≥3:1.
  No new JS shipped by this diff (`git diff master -- web/static/js/` is
  empty) and no `autofocus` attribute added, so no keyboard trap and no
  focus theft is introduced.
  PASS.

